# Spot welding: a ceramic disc (C1) in the vise, its leads down; a
# second (C2) brought to C1's lead 2, 6 mm from the body, from a clear
# side, and welded by arm C's capacitor discharge, in the window of
# their copper-clad steel; then the LED (D1, a semiconductor) brought to
# C1's lead 1 the same way. Welded as it is, the LED would take the
# discharge's transient, so the weld would be refused: an arm clips the
# LED's lead to ground between its body and the lap first, and the weld
# is made. The tools back away and arm A lets go: the three stay in
# the vise as one, welded.
reset circuit=weld
tool A tweezers
pick A C1 grasp=body
place A C1 at=0,0,-20
vise close
release A C1
pick A C2 grasp=body
lift A mm=80
move A to=20.08,0,-5.746
align A C2.1.tip to=C1.2.6 gap=0.1
tool C welder
weld C at=C1.2+C2.1 energy=8
back C mm=60
release A C2
lift A mm=40
pick A D1 grasp=body
lift A mm=80
move A to=-16.27,0,3.554
align A D1.1.tip to=C1.1.6 gap=0.1
tool B clip
clip B on=D1.1 at=8
weld C at=C1.1+D1.1 energy=8
inspect C1.1+D1.1
back C mm=60
back B mm=60
release A D1
lift A mm=40
